## Bug Hunt Summary — PRD §9.9 Validation Gate Semantics (Session 011)

I performed a creative, adversarial end-to-end validation of the §9.9 delta across all four implementation layers.

**What I tested (all correct & robust):**
- **Detector** (`gate-semantics.ts`) — 16-case adversarial probe: all 4 canonical negated-existence forms neutralized; negated content/ambiguous/compound/`[[ ]]`/full-path all execute normally (G2.2/G2.3). Zero dangerous false positives — shell semantics guarantee the matched prefixes are always negation.
- **Executor integration** (`prp-executor.ts #runValidationGates`) — neutralized shape mirrors manual skip, BashMCP not invoked, aggregation counts skipped as passed, fix-retry excludes neutralized gates, watchdog terminal-abort unaffected. Confirmed it's the only mechanical gate-execution path (no bypass).
- **Runtime effectiveness** — the §9.9-edited monolithic `prompts.ts` **is** what reaches the model (via `agent-factory` system prompts and the split wrapper that embeds the base); no shadowing, no contradictory guidance.
- **Docs/log** — README, ARCHITECTURE, PROMPTS.md mirror all synced; runtime log reason matches PRD G2.1 wording verbatim.
- **Verification** — src-only `tsc` clean (exit 0); 40 + 84 + 11 tests pass. (The 680 `tsc` diagnostics are pre-existing in test files, excluded from build, none touching §9.9.)

**One real finding (minor):**
- **BUG-001** — PRD §9.9.2 G1.4 mandates the throwaway-survival instruction in *both* the Blueprint **and** Builder prompts. The Builder carries it (`prompts.ts:~750`), but the Blueprint (`PRP_BLUEPRINT_PROMPT`, gate-construction rules at `prompts.ts:285-293`) only enumerates G1.1/G1.2/G1.3/G1.5 — no G1.4. Functional impact is low (the Builder carries the Coder rule and G1.3 already blocks the harmful gate), so §9.9.3 acceptance remains satisfiable, but the literal dual-prompt requirement is only half-met.

